# BetterTwitch for webOS

A modified Twitch client for LG webOS TVs.

The main goal of this project is to make Twitch more usable on webOS while keeping the app lightweight enough for older TVs.

## Features

* Ad blocking
* HLS proxy by default
* Up to 1440p when the stream provides it
* Audio Only quality
* 7TV emotes
* BTTV emotes
* FFZ emotes
* Channel points
* Chat overlay
* Low latency mode
* Disabled unnecessary animations
* Various performance improvements for TVs with limited RAM

## Quality

The app uses a proxy for Twitch HLS playback instead of relying on the default stream request.

Available quality depends on what Twitch and the proxy return for the current channel. If 1440p is available, it can be selected directly from the quality menu.

Audio Only is also provided as an HLS playlist option.

## Installation

### Homebrew Channel

Add the following repository to Homebrew Channel:

tinyurl.com/twitchmod10


After adding the repository, install BetterTwitch and launch it normally.

### Manual installation

Download the latest .ipk from the Releases page and install it using your preferred webOS installation tool.



The application package itself is published in GitHub Releases.

## Compatibility

The application is intended for LG webOS TVs.

Actual playback quality and available features may vary depending on:

* TV model and webOS version
* Twitch stream
* Available Twitch renditions
* Network connection
* Proxy availability

Older TVs may also have limited RAM, so some parts of the application are intentionally kept as simple as possible.


